    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe `Regions` class itself is well-formed (private constructor, immutable `Map.of`, `getOrDefault`, a dedicated named `UNKNOWN` constant) \u2014 a lookup table is genuinely cleaner as its own class than inlined into the mapper expression, so extracting it is the right call. The problem is where it landed and what it claims.\n\nFindings:\n\n1. **Wrong package \u2014 placed among OfficeFloor function helpers, but no function uses it.** `rest.function.common` holds helpers for the function pipeline (`Lookups` for Load functions, `RespondWithNoContent` as a function). `Regions`'s sole consumer is `OwnerMapper` (confirmed by grep \u2014 nothing in `rest/function/**` references it). A maintainer looking for mapper-support code would not expect it under `rest.function.common`, and a maintainer browsing that package would wrongly assume it's part of the function layer. Move it next to its consumer \u2014 e.g. a helper in the `mapper` package (`org.springframework.samples.petclinic.mapper`) \u2014 which also shortens the fully-qualified reference in the `@Mapping` expression.\n\n2. **Javadoc is factually wrong.** The class comment says \"shared by the owner functions\" and the `CITY_REGION` comment echoes the function framing, but it is used by the mapper, and by exactly one caller \u2014 it is neither \"shared\" nor used by any function. Reword to describe its actual role (city\u2192region derivation for `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`). This mismatch is the kind of thing that misleads the next maintainer about the code's role.\n\nBoth are localized and don't affect the mapper wiring or the OpenAPI addition, which are fine.",
